To create this interactive webpage using PHP, you'll need to use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (or jQuery) for the frontend part. Here's a simple example of how you can achieve this:

1. HTML (index.php):
```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Interactive Square</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
    <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="container">
        <div id="drag-square" class="square white-square"></div>
        <div id="static-square" class="square gray-square"></div>
    </div>
    <button id="reset-btn">Reset</button>
</body>
</html>
```
1. CSS (styles.css):
```css
#container {
    position: relative;
    width: 80%;
    margin: auto;
}

.square {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    position: absolute;
    border: 2px solid black;
}

.white-square {
    background-color: white;
}

.gray-square {
    background-color: gray;
    border-color: red;
}
```
1. JavaScript (script.js):
```javascript
$().ready(function () {
    var $dragSquare = $('#drag-square');
    var $staticSquare = $('#static-square');
    var dragSquareColor = 'white-square';

    $dragSquare.mousedown(function () {
        $dragSquare.addClass('dragging');
        $staticSquare.bind('mouseup', function () {
            $dragSquare.removeClass('dragging');
            $staticSquare.unbind('mouseup');
        });
    });

    $dragSquare.mouseenter(function () {
        $dragSquare.addClass('yellow-square');
    });

    $dragSquare.mouseleave(function () {
        $dragSquare.removeClass('yellow-square');
    });

    $dragSquare.draggable({
        handle: this,
        start: function () {
            dragSquareColor = $dragSquare.attr('class').replace(' dragging', '');
            $dragSquare.removeClass(dragSquareColor);
            $dragSquare.addClass('blue-square');
        },
        stop: function () {
            $dragSquare.removeClass('dragging blue-square');
            $dragSquare.addClass(dragSquareColor);
        }
    });

    $staticSquare.droppable({
        tolerance: 'touch',
        drop: function (event, ui) {
            $(this).css('background-color', 'green');
            $dragSquare.addClass('green-square');
        }
    });

    $('#reset-btn').click(function () {
        $dragSquare.removeClass('dragging blue-square yellow-square green-square');
        $dragSquare.addClass('white-square');
        $staticSquare.css('background-color', 'gray');
    });
});
```
Make sure to copy the above files (index.php, styles.css, and script.js) into the web server root directory (e.g., `/var/www/html/`).

In this example, jQuery and jQuery UI are used for the draggable functionality. The gray square's color changes to green when the draggable square is dropped on top of it. A reset button is also provided to revert the squares back to their initial settings.

